# Maximum Subarray — Kadane's Algorithm

## 1. Core Pattern

Kadane's Algorithm

## 2. Missing Trick

If the current `sum` becomes negative, discard it by resetting `sum = 0`.

A negative previous sum will only reduce the sum of any future subarray.

```java
if (sum < 0) {
    sum = 0;
}
```

## 3. Flawed Approach

I was correctly calculating `sum` and comparing it with `maxSum`, but I didn't realize that carrying a **negative previous sum** into the next subarray is harmful.

I was missing the idea of **starting fresh when the running sum becomes negative**.
